{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387400-on-evolving-paradigms","id":1387400,"title":"On Evolving Paradigms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-10T20:02:33-07:00","id":1387400,"title":"On Evolving Paradigms","content":"The Technocracy Reloaded Kickstarter has got me re-reading my other books, and something occurred to me: what's stopping a mage from learning and incorporating aspects of foreign paradigms into their own? Beyond just switching their focus/allegiance (Mage 20, p.339)? Suppose a Vebenae technopagan starts using hypertech along with more 'traditional' practices; would their original focus be inhibited just as if they had switched their focus wholesale? Or what about an orphan or Hollow One whose 'catch as catch can' approach to magick just uses whatever they can find in a sort of &quot;all things are true' paradigm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T21:14:31-07:00","id":1387406,"title":"","content":"Rules-wise, there's a suggested limit of (I think) three Practices per mage; it's not a hard rule, and I tend to enforce it more through the Associated Abilities (see Do for an extreme version of this) than through a hard count of Practices. That is, you can learn and use as many Practices as your Abilities will allow. <br /> <br /> Some Practices have more stringent Ability Requirements than others, with Gutter Magic and Do being the extreme examples: Gutter Magic (the \u201cPractice\u201d of the Hollow Ones and many Orphans) doesn't place any Ability requirements on the mage, while Do has an elaborate system of, what is it, eight different Abilities you're supposed to train in? As a rule of thumb, I identify one signature Ability for each Practice and require one dot in the signature Ability and three dots spread out across the other Associated Abilities. <br /> <br /> Not that I've ever had to enforce those requirements; players generally <i>want</i> to put this into Associated Abilities, as those tend to be the ones used by a given Practice for Abilities assisting Magick. <br /> <br /> What these Ability \u201crequirements\u201d do is to provide a way to judge how similar two Practices are: if they share a lot of Associated Abilities, chances are that a mage who is into one of the Practices won't need to learn much before he can get into the other one. Conversely, if the Associated Practices have little or nothing in common, it's going to take a lot more dedication to study and training to engage in both Practices.<br /> <br /> And of course there are three standard requirements that Paradigm, Practice, and Instruments need to be consistent: in addition to the above stuff about Associated Abilities, adding a Practice requires that the new Practice be consistent with the mage's Paradigm, and that some of the mage's Instruments are associated with the new Practice. <br /> <br /> That latter requirement can be surprisingly tricky to manage if the new Practice doesn't have any Associated Instruments in common with the existing ones \u2014 largely because of a highly technical issue of each mage having seven Instruments that are (usually) discarded as Arete increases until there are none. Gaining a Practice can't add to the number of Instruments you have, lest it throw the progression of discarding Instruments out of whack. So when you try to add a Practice that doesn't work with any of the Instruments that the mage has already selected, some added effort needs to be made to \u201cswap out\u201d some of the existing Instruments for ones suited to the new Practice. <br /> <br /> Either that, or amend the schedule for discarding Instruments from one (or two, in the case of technomancers) per dot of Arete to one <i>per Practice</i> per dot of Arete, and say that every mage gets seven Instruments per Practice. But then you need to address the matter of overlapping Instruments, and the whole thing gets messy really fast. <br /> <br /> On the other end, it's surprisingly easier to ensure that your Paradigm is compatible with all of your Practices: a Paradigm can be, and usually is, a composite Paradigm, so long as the component Paradigms don't clash with each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-11-2020, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T20:19:00-07:00","id":1387877,"title":"","content":"The seven instruments issue was brought up in the M20 Book of Secrets (p.171) if that helps you any, but this was very helpful. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}